<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;netstandard2.1</TargetFrameworks>
    <LangVersion>8.0</LangVersion> <!-- Set C# language version -->
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable> <!-- Enable nullable reference types -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile> <!-- Enable XML documentation generation -->
    <DocumentationFile>bin\$(Configuration)\$(TargetFramework)\$(AssemblyName).xml</DocumentationFile> <!-- Specify the documentation file path -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);1591</NoWarn> <!-- Suppress warnings for missing XML comments -->

    <!-- NuGet Package Information -->
    <PackageId>CSPR.Cloud.Net</PackageId>
    <Version>4.3.0</Version>
    <Authors>msanlisavas</Authors>
    <Description>A .NET client library for interacting with the CSPR Cloud API, providing access to Casper blockchain data for both Mainnet and Testnet environments.</Description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/msanlisavas/CSPR.Cloud.Net</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/msanlisavas/CSPR.Cloud.Net</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>Casper;Blockchain;CSPR;Cloud;API;Client</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v4.3.0 — FIX (wire correctness, every item live-verified against mainnet and testnet): seven model properties bound to JSON keys the API has never emitted, so they deserialized to null (or, when non-nullable, to 0) on every row, indistinguishable from a real absent value. UndelegationData was wrong in three ways at once: DelegatorIdentifier bound delegator_identifier but the wire name is staker_identifier; EraOfCreation bound era_of_creation but it is era_id; and DelegatorIdentifierTypeId bound delegator_identifier_type_id but it is withdrawal_type_id — being a non-nullable int it read 0 on every row, silently reporting every purse withdrawal as a public-key withdrawal while its identifier was null. ValidatorPerformanceData.AverageScore bound average_score but the endpoint emits score; because that type is also ValidatorData.AveragePerformance and BidderData.AveragePerformance, every caller who requested the average_performance includer got a null score too. DEPRECATED (kept so callers still compile, to be removed in the next major): AccountData.UndelegatedBalance (the API emits undelegating_balance, already bound by UndelegatingBalance); UndelegationData.AccountInfo and CentralizedAccountInfo (that endpoint supports only the validator_account_info includer — verified by control request); ValidatorData.PendingUnstakingAmount; SwapData.Token0FtRate/Token1FtRate (never returned even when their includer is requested — the API silently ignores unknown includer names, so the includer name itself is likely wrong, pending confirmation with the CSPR.cloud team); and the four ContractResponse&lt;T&gt; envelope properties, whose values the API nests inside data and which ContractPackageData already binds correctly. Also: the UndelegationData test fixtures were rebuilt from captured live payloads — the previous ones invented keys the endpoint has never returned, which is why these bugs survived. No breaking changes; affected properties simply start carrying their real values. Earlier: v4.2.1 fixed x402 ValidAfter/ValidBefore wire typing; v4.2.0 added CasperCloudX402Client; v4.1.0 added CancellationToken to every REST method; v4.0.x made money values decimal.</PackageReleaseNotes>

  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Folder Include="Icon\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="8.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.3" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="CSPR.Cloud.Net.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
